hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"370","Muhammad bin Isa said, by Salamah, meaning Ibn al-Fadl, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was He introduced it, but people gather to pray at its appointed time without an invitation, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, intended to make a trumpet Like the trumpet of the Jews with which they call for their prayers. Then he disliked it, then he ordered the bell to be carved to be sounded with it for the Muslims to pray, while They were like that. Abdullah bin Zaid bin Abdul Rabbo, brother of Al-Harith bin Al-Khazraj, was shown the call, so he came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted me, and he said to him: O Messenger of God, a pilgrim went around me this night. A man wearing two green clothes passed by me, carrying a gong in his hand. So I said: O Abdullah, do you sell this bell? He said: What do you do with it? I said: We call him to prayer, and he said: Shall I not guide you to something better than that? I said: What is it? He said: “You say: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness That Muhammad is the Messenger of God, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, hail to prayer, hail to prayer, hail to success, hail to success, God is great, God is great Akbar, there is no god but Allah. Then he delayed it for a long time, then he said: Just as he said: And he made it the odd string, except that the prayer has begun. The prayer has already begun, by God. “The greatest, God is the greatest, there is no god but God.” When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, told her about it, he said: It is a true vision, God willing, so rise up. With Bilal, say it to him, for he has a more beautiful voice than you. When Bilal called the call to prayer, Omar ibn al-Khattab heard about it while he was in his house, so he went out to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was pulling his cloak and saying: O Prophet of God, by the One who has sent you with the truth, I have seen something like what he saw, so he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Praise be to God, for that is proven.”"
"371","Muhammad bin Yahya told me, Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told me, my father told me, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, Muhammad bin Ibrahim bin Al-Harith al-Taymi told me, On the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Zaid bin Abdul Rabbo, Abu Abdullah bin Zaid told me, he said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered He greeted the gong, and it was made to be sounded for the people in the gathering for prayer.” He mentioned the hadith in its length, like the hadith of Salamah ibn al-Fadl."
"372","He said: I heard Muhammad bin Yahya saying: There is no news in the reports of Abdullah bin Zaid regarding the story of the call to prayer more authentic than this, because Muhammad bin Abdul Allah bin Zaid heard it from his father, and Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila did not hear it from Abdullah bin Zaid."
"373","Muhammad bin Ali told us after his hadith, he said: Yaqoub bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, my father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Then Muhammad mentioned Bin Muslim bin Abdullah bin Shihab Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd bin Abdul Rabbo with this The news, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “This is a true vision, God willing.” Then he ordered the call to prayer, and it was Bilal. Abu Bakr’s servant gives the call to prayer.”"
"374","Bundar told us, from Muhammad bin Ja’far, from Shu’bah, who said: I heard Abu Ja’far, speaking, on the authority of Muslim bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: “At the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the call to prayer was only given twice and the iqama once, except that he used to say: The prayer has begun. The prayer began, so when we heard that, we performed ablution and then went out.” Muhammad said: Shu`bah said: I have not heard from Abu Ja`far other than this hadith. It is narrated by Bundar, it is narrated by Yahya, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, on the authority of Muslim bin Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Ibn Umar, the same."
